WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.222
Soon Valjean's eyes grew accustomed to the darkness.

2
00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:25.025
He had entered the sewer from a grate along the street, and the faint light from above penetrated

3
00:00:25.065 --> 00:00:25.505
the tunnel.

4
00:00:26.666 --> 00:00:29.788
Valjean laid Marius down while he rested for a moment.

5
00:00:30.332 --> 00:00:35.296
Then he slung the wounded man across his back again and set off through the tunnel.

6
00:00:36.356 --> 00:00:39.118
Marius was gravely ill and unconscious.

7
00:00:39.959 --> 00:00:42.360
Perhaps Valjean had no chance of saving him.

8
00:00:43.441 --> 00:00:47.884
Valjean had been walking for about half an hour when he saw his shadow in front of him.

9
00:00:48.425 --> 00:00:50.186
Puzzled, he turned around.

10
00:00:51.306 --> 00:00:56.070
In the distance he saw some torchlight, and behind that some people were moving.

11
00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.132
Valjean stood with his back against the wall.

12
00:01:00.148 --> 00:01:04.350
He must escape from these people even though he did not know their identities.

13
00:01:05.311 --> 00:01:10.213
In fact, they were policemen who had been ordered to search the sewers for rebels.

14
00:01:11.114 --> 00:01:15.336
Luckily for Valjean, he could see the police better than they could see him.

15
00:01:16.677 --> 00:01:22.300
They had heard his footsteps, but now that he had stopped moving, they decided that nobody was there.

16
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.323
Just to be sure, one policeman fired a shot in Valjean's direction.

17
00:01:28.023 --> 00:01:29.544
It hit the arch over his head.

18
00:01:30.144 --> 00:01:34.668
Valjean remained motionless until the men turned around and disappeared in the dark.

19
00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:39.011
Meanwhile another chase had been going on aboveground.

20
00:01:39.652 --> 00:01:45.337
A policeman had been following a suspicious character, hoping that the man might lead him to a band

21
00:01:45.377 --> 00:01:46.017
of criminals.

22
00:01:47.238 --> 00:01:52.242
As they approached the docks on the Seine River, the man disappeared behind a rubbish pile.

23
00:01:53.223 --> 00:01:58.868
The policeman quickened his pace, but after passing the rubbish pile, he stopped in amazement.

24
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.162
The man he'd been pursuing was nowhere to be seen.

25
00:02:03.262 --> 00:02:06.604
Then he noticed a grate covering a wide, dark opening.

26
00:02:07.344 --> 00:02:10.586
Unlike the one near the barricade, this grate was locked.

27
00:02:10.606 --> 00:02:12.147
"Of course!"

28
00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:13.468
said the policeman.

29
00:02:13.488 --> 00:02:15.329
"He went into the sewer.

30
00:02:16.089 --> 00:02:18.531
Somewhere he must have found a key to open the grate."

31
00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:25.895
After Valjean's encounter with the police, he continued to walk for hours with Marius on his back.

32
00:02:26.475 --> 00:02:27.656
He was very tired.

33
00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.523
When he came to a large air hole, he laid Marius on the ground.

34
00:02:33.223 --> 00:02:38.046
In the light, he could see that Marius was still breathing despite his terrible wounds.

35
00:02:39.047 --> 00:02:42.730
Valjean searched Marius' pockets and found a scrap of bread to eat.

36
00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.753
He also found the note with Marius' name and Monsieur Gillenormand's address.

37
00:02:47.773 --> 00:02:52.276
"Now I know who he is and where to take him," said Valjean.

38
00:02:53.097 --> 00:02:56.159
But at that moment, Valjean had no idea where they were.

39
00:02:56.839 --> 00:03:01.383
He pushed on and soon felt the stone under his feet replaced with mud.

40
00:03:01.403 --> 00:03:06.306
"This is like a swamp, but I can't go back," said Valjean.

41
00:03:06.907 --> 00:03:09.769
"Marius is dying, and I must press on."

42
00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:15.373
The water rose up to his armpits, and yet he still kept going forward.

43
00:03:16.053 --> 00:03:20.517
Valjean sank deeper and struggled to keep Marius' head above water.

44
00:03:22.018 --> 00:03:24.980
At last Valjean felt something solid under his feet.

45
00:03:25.544 --> 00:03:29.626
The path before him gradually sloped uphill and the water receded.

46
00:03:30.347 --> 00:03:34.709
When he reached a dry spot, Valjean sank to his knees, exhausted.

47
00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.451
But Valjean managed to stand once more.

48
00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:42.733
He had carried Marius only a hundred paces when he saw a wall.

49
00:03:43.274 --> 00:03:46.615
Valjean looked to his left and saw a light far away.

50
00:03:46.635 --> 00:03:48.376
"There's an opening!"

51
00:03:49.037 --> 00:03:50.858
Valjean no longer felt exhausted.

52
00:03:51.418 --> 00:03:54.920
He practically ran to the outlet, but then he stopped.

53
00:03:55.964 --> 00:03:59.245
It was covered with a grate, and a sturdy lock held it shut.

54
00:03:59.866 --> 00:04:03.067
Beyond the grate, Valjean could see docks and the river.

55
00:04:03.087 --> 00:04:06.148
"It's all over," said Valjean.

56
00:04:06.168 --> 00:04:08.249
"We're trapped in this place."

57
00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.751
He put his head in his hands and thought of Cosette.

58
00:04:12.831 --> 00:04:18.494
Suddenly someone laid a hand on Valjean's shoulder and said, "You want to split what's in this guy's

59
00:04:18.594 --> 00:04:23.956
pockets?" Valjean looked up and saw Thenardier standing before him.

60
00:04:24.556 --> 00:04:29.938
They gazed at each other for a moment, and Valjean realized that Thenardier did not recognize him.

61
00:04:29.958 --> 00:04:34.919
"You've obviously killed this guy and need to get out of here," Thenardier went on.

62
00:04:34.939 --> 00:04:37.580
"And I have a key to the grate."

63
00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:44.322
Valjean nodded, but said nothing as Thenardier busied himself searching Marius' pockets.

64
00:04:45.502 --> 00:04:48.663
"That old man is an odd fellow," Thenardier thought.

65
00:04:48.683 --> 00:04:51.504
"There's something strange going on here.

66
00:04:52.468 --> 00:04:54.890
I'm going to tear a strip from this young guy's coat.

67
00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.572
You never know when something like that will come in handy."

68
00:04:59.553 --> 00:05:05.217
Thenardier removed a few coins from Marius' pockets and kept them all, lying to Valjean.

69
00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.439
"He didn't have any money.

70
00:05:07.919 --> 00:05:09.861
Not much point in killing him, was there?

71
00:05:10.521 --> 00:05:12.342
Here, I'll let you out now."

72
00:05:13.343 --> 00:05:17.166
With that, he put the key in the lock and opened the grate for Valjean.

73
00:05:17.186 --> 00:05:19.928
"Good luck!"

74
00:05:20.508 --> 00:05:24.471
said Thenardier as he locked the grate again and disappeared inside the sewer.

75
00:05:25.392 --> 00:05:28.114
Valjean stood for a moment breathing in the fresh air.

76
00:05:28.775 --> 00:05:31.237
Then he carried Marius over to the docks.

77
00:05:32.478 --> 00:05:37.782
He dipped his hand into the river and let a few drops of water fall on Marius' face.

78
00:05:38.503 --> 00:05:41.606
The unconscious man stirred but did not open his eyes.

79
00:05:42.586 --> 00:05:45.549
Suddenly Valjean heard footsteps behind him.

80
00:05:46.329 --> 00:05:49.152
He turned and there stood Javert.

81
00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:54.144
It was Javert who had been pursing Thenardier until he disappeared into the sewer!

82
00:05:54.164 --> 00:05:55.585
"Who are you?"

83
00:05:55.945 --> 00:05:59.808
Javert asked the mud-covered man kneeling on the dock next to Marius.

84
00:05:59.828 --> 00:06:01.790
"Don't you recognize me?

85
00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.451
I'm Valjean."

86
00:06:04.432 --> 00:06:06.133
Javert stared into his eyes.

87
00:06:06.894 --> 00:06:10.077
"What are you doing here and who is this injured man?"

88
00:06:10.097 --> 00:06:16.062
"I've considered myself your prisoner since I gave you my address this morning," said Valjean.

89
00:06:16.082 --> 00:06:22.533
"Do with me what you will, but first help me carry this boy to his grandfather's house."

90
00:06:23.774 --> 00:06:25.655
Javert studied Marius' face.

91
00:06:26.355 --> 00:06:27.816
"He was in the barricade, wasn't he?

92
00:06:28.436 --> 00:06:29.476
His name is Marius."

93
00:06:30.437 --> 00:06:35.399
Valjean felt in Marius' pocket and pulled out the paper with his grandfather's address.

94
00:06:35.999 --> 00:06:38.900
"We must take him here, quickly before he dies."

95
00:06:39.941 --> 00:06:45.103
At Monsieur Gillenormand's house, a servant helped the two men carry Marius inside.

96
00:06:46.243 --> 00:06:52.501
As they got back into the carriage again, Valjean said, "Inspector Javert, grant me one more thing.

97
00:06:53.221 --> 00:06:55.362
Allow me to go home before you arrest me."

98
00:06:56.462 --> 00:07:00.343
"Fine," said Javert, "but only for a few minutes.

99
00:07:00.964 --> 00:07:02.284
I'll wait for you in the street."

100
00:07:03.464 --> 00:07:07.385
At his apartment building, Valjean headed upstairs with a heavy heart.

101
00:07:08.046 --> 00:07:13.067
His life was over now that Javert had caught him; he was going back to prison.

102
00:07:13.907 --> 00:07:18.393
But he needed to say good-bye to Cosette and tell her that he'd found Marius.

103
00:07:20.073 --> 00:07:23.454
On the landing Valjean paused to gaze out the window.

104
00:07:24.214 --> 00:07:27.175
He leaned out further and looked up and down the street.

105
00:07:27.715 --> 00:07:30.396
To his amazement, Javert was gone!

106
00:07:31.296 --> 00:07:35.557
Javert walked slowly away from Valjean's house and headed for the river.

107
00:07:36.277 --> 00:07:40.679
He had been in turmoil ever since Valjean had spared his life that morning.

108
00:07:41.679 --> 00:07:47.873
Javert felt something new and horrible penetrating his soul: admiration for a convict.

109
00:07:48.653 --> 00:07:53.614
Here was a criminal who was compassionate, who took pity rather than vengeance.

110
00:07:54.675 --> 00:07:57.535
Surely this man could not really exist, but he did.

111
00:07:58.696 --> 00:08:02.197
Javert had reached the river now, his thoughts torturing him.

112
00:08:02.857 --> 00:08:09.499
His whole belief system—what was right, what was wrong—had been turned upside down by Jean Valjean.

113
00:08:10.519 --> 00:08:15.943
He felt that he had failed somehow, that it would be impossible to continue doing his job.

114
00:08:16.964 --> 00:08:21.307
Javert jumped into the river and was swept away by the current.
